# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_github_http_keepalive.py" "GITHUB HTTP KEEP-ALIVE GATE: PASS" "github http keep-alive" "github http keep-alive (thread-local pool · max-age recycle · kill switch · reset-on-error)" "GITHUB HTTP KEEP-ALIVE: GitHubREST._urlopen reuses ONE persistent http.client.HTTPSConnection per (host,port,scheme) per worker thread (saves the ~80-150 ms TCP+TLS handshake on every call) — proves: (a) REUSE (two sequential calls on one thread reuse the same conn), (b) THREAD-LOCAL (concurrent threads each get their own conn — http.client.HTTPSConnection is NOT thread-safe), (c) MAX-AGE recycle (a cached conn past VERIPSA_HTTP_KEEPALIVE_MAX_AGE_SECONDS is closed + replaced before reuse), (d) KILL SWITCH (VERIPSA_HTTP_KEEPALIVE=0 reverts to per-call urllib.urlopen, the legacy path the resilience gate already proves), (e) RESET on a wire error (a connect/send failure closes + drops the cached conn — no stale-keepalive replay), (f) HTTPError on 5xx does NOT drop the conn (HTTP-level errors are not connection-level)" 16
